Keep the Claude permission hook's bearer fresh so questions reach the web UI.

Claude's AskUserQuestion and plan prompts reach the web UI through the
PermissionRequest hook, which posts to the server with the bearer in the
bridge's permission_hook.json. Upstream stopped refreshing that file when it
moved the policy hook onto the runner's relay, but left this hook on it. A
sandbox runner's bearer lasts 30 minutes, and the hook has no credential to
mint a new one, so after that the server answered 401, the hook gave up, and
the question waited in Claude's terminal while the web UI showed a spinner.
The runner again rewrites the file every minute, as upstream did before, and
the hook retries a 401 with the file's newer bearer before re-minting.
Upstream fix to backport; delete this patch once upstream ships one.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0012-environment-exit-node.patch.

